# --- the vLLM-Omni comparison arm --------------------------------------------
# This is env.sh's IWM_OMNI_PY (.venv-omni). It exists only to run serve_omni_arm.py, the
# external reference arm that measures a shipped third-party optimization against ours.
#
# A THIRD LOCK, FOR THE SAME REASON THERE IS A SECOND ONE.
# server-requirements.in is pinned to lingbot-va/requirements.txt exactly, because the served
# baseline has to be the upstream one. vllm-omni cannot live there:
#
#   * vllm-omni >= 0.22 pins `diffusers==0.38.0`; the server pins 0.36.0. Only 0.20.0 accepts
#     0.36, and 0.20.0 does not contain PromptEmbedCache -- so no single version both satisfies
#     the server's pins and carries the component under test.
#   * `import vllm_omni` requires `vllm`, an UNDECLARED dependency (absent from vllm-omni's
#     requires_dist, yet vllm_omni/model_executor/models/registry.py:1 imports it), and vllm
#     pins `torch==2.11.0` against the server's 2.9.0.
#
# Changing either would change served numerics, and RESULTS.md's appendix records the cost: a
# diffusers change reroutes autoencoder_kl_wan and invalidates the 91.6% baseline. So this arm
# gets its own environment and talks over the websocket, exactly as the RoboTwin client
# (torch 2.4) already coexists with the server (torch 2.9). See env.sh: "Never try to merge
# these."
#
# CONSEQUENCE FOR MEASUREMENT: because the stack differs, absolute ms from this arm are NOT
# comparable to arms run under IWM_SERVER_PY. Only the within-env delta (D_base - D) is.
# run_omni_arm.sh measures both of its arms here so that cannot be violated by accident.
#
# Regenerate the lock after editing:
#   uv pip compile omni-arm-requirements.in --python-version 3.10 -o omni-arm-requirements.txt

vllm-omni==0.26.0
vllm

# The LingBot-VA server's own runtime needs, deliberately UNPINNED: this environment is not
# trying to reproduce the server's pins, it is letting vllm-omni resolve freely and then hosting
# the server on whatever that produces. It works -- the server runs unmodified on
# transformers 5.x / numpy 2.x / diffusers 0.38.
transformers
accelerate
einops
easydict
tqdm
imageio[ffmpeg]
websockets
msgpack
opencv-python
matplotlib
ftfy
safetensors
Pillow
numpy
